WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.791
AJA HAMMERLY: Let me
show you how to create

00:00:01.791 --> 00:00:03.200
a compute instance with Fog.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.030
Fog is a cloud services
library for Ruby.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.640
Use it with Google
Cloud Platform.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.440
You'll use the Fog Google Gem.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.070
I'm using a .fog file
for authentication.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.760
Here's the code I'm going to
use to create an instance.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.670
First, I connect,
then I create a disk,

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.050
and wait for it to be ready.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.642
After that I create a
server using that disk,

00:00:21.642 --> 00:00:23.350
and then wait for the
server to be ready.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.270
When the server is
ready, I can SSH into it

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.930
because I've set up my SSH keys.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.054
Let's see the code running.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.440
To learn more about Fog, Google,
and Google Compute Engine,

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.110
look at the links in
the video description.

